&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is an opportunity to work for a remote-first company. Only applicants living in British Columbia will be considered, with preference given to Victoria, BC.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driven by &lt;strong&gt;PLAYER OBSESSION&lt;/strong&gt;, we look to craft unparalleled gaming experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OWNERSHIP&lt;/strong&gt; is our compass, propelling us to deliver exceptional results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a spirit of &lt;strong&gt;RESOURCEFULNESS&lt;/strong&gt;, we fearlessly tackle challenges and defy limitations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driven by the ethos of &lt;strong&gt;CONTINUOUS IMPROVEMENT&lt;/strong&gt;, we foster a culture of perpetual learning and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Kano&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kano is an independent game studio that has been building and running live games for over 18 years. Our games have long-running player communities, mature economies, live events, web and mobile platforms, and real business complexity behind them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a small, remote-first team that is all-in on AI. We use it across the company, from engineering to finance to marketing. People here can make a visible impact quickly, so we look for people who take ownership, learn fast, and like replacing &quot;the way it&#39;s always been done.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll use AI tools and automation to run and modernize Kano&#39;s systems: the cloud infrastructure behind our live games, and the IT the rest of the company relies on. You&#39;ll join our Operations team, which looks after every Kano game, our internal systems and the projects coming next, and help keep all of it reliable, secure and cost-effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Keeping our games running comes first. Our infrastructure has grown over 18 years and runs on a mix of EC2, ECS containers and serverless. You&#39;ll bring fresh eyes to making it simpler, safer and less manual, and you&#39;ll have real room to make those changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Right Person…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses AI tools like Claude Code, Cursor or ChatGPT for real technical work, can show something they&#39;ve automated or improved, and tests and validates the results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wants to build AI-assisted tools that take repetitive work off the team&#39;s plate, with human review where it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has solid fundamentals and a hands-on approach: verifies their work, troubleshoots methodically and knows when to ask for help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Would rather fix the root cause than patch the same problem twice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-assisted workflows for operations, such as alert triage, incident summaries, first-draft root-cause analyses and runbook upkeep.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI coding agents to write and refactor infrastructure code and scripts, with testing and review before anything reaches production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up access controls for our internal AI agents and tools: least-privilege credentials, audit logging and approvals for production changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trial new tools and services, and recommend what to adopt and what to retire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure &amp;amp; Cloud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run and improve the Linux servers and AWS infrastructure behind our live games (EC2, ECS, Lambda, VPC, IAM, S3, Route 53, Systems Manager), managed with Terraform, Chef, and Ansible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry out upgrades, patching and migrations onto containers or managed services, keeping disruption to players to a minimum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support our Docker and ECS services and the pipelines that ship them (GitLab CI, AWS CodeDeploy, Fastlane).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability &amp;amp; Data&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain monitoring, alerting and logging (CloudWatch, InfluxDB, Grafana, Graylog) to catch problems before players notice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look after our MySQL, MongoDB, Redis and Memcached services: backups, regular restore tests, upgrades and routine issues, working through complex replication or performance problems with the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After onboarding, join the on-call rotation. You&#39;ll start with triage and escalation alongside experienced teammates, take on more as you get comfortable, and contribute to incident reviews so issues don&#39;t recur.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company IT &amp;amp; Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the IT behind a remote team: staff accounts and access, VPN and internal network services, onboarding and offboarding, and help for non-technical teammates. Automate the requests that keep coming back.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain least-privilege access and MFA, apply security patches, review logs and support compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find AWS cost savings and implement them, such as right-sizing and removing unused resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writes clear documentation and explains technical issues in plain language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years running production infrastructure in systems administration, IT operations, DevOps, SRE or platform engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux administration and a methodical approach to troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS fundamentals: EC2, ECS, Lambda, VPC networking, IAM, S3 and CloudWatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Networking fundamentals: TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, VPNs and load balancing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as code (e.g. Terraform) and scripting in Bash, Python or Ruby.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Docker, and running containerized services in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running relational and/or NoSQL databases in production, including backups, restores and upgrades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good operational judgment: testing changes, following review processes and knowing when to escalate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular, hands-on use of AI tools for technical work, and the judgment to check what they produce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building AI agents, LLM-powered tools, or automations using APIs, MCP or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MongoDB, Redis or Memcached at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chef, Ansible, GitLab CI, AWS CodeDeploy or Fastlane.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;InfluxDB, Grafana or Graylog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS cost optimization, including Savings Plans and Reserved Instances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting staff IT for a remote team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in games or other always-on consumer services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$85,000 - $100,00 CAD&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The listed range reflects potential earnings for this role. Actual pay depends on experience and skills, and most hires start near the midpoint.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kano is a remote-first workplace with an in-person attendance requirement 2-6 times a year.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive wages determined by market research&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncapped profit share program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health, dental and vision benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 weeks vacation to start&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid holiday shutdown in December&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 paid Care Days per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Yearly Continuous Improvement allowance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A results-driven company with a compassionate culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on game projects that are enjoyed by millions of players worldwide!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to make a difference. Have an idea? Talk directly with leadership about it instead of running through layers of bureaucracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Kano&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since inception, Kano has released twelve gaming titles (seven of which are live serviced today), with over 35 million downloads and close to $100M in sales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bootstrapped in 2008, and achieving profitability in 2009, Kano continues to grow its team, game portfolio and player base as an independent gaming studio, with hit games like &lt;a href=&quot;https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=monster.country.idle&amp;amp;hl=en_CA&amp;amp;gl=US&quot;&gt;Mob Wars&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.kanoapps.bz&amp;amp;hl=en_CA&amp;amp;gl=US&quot;&gt;Idle Distiller&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=monster.country.idle&amp;amp;hl=en_CA&amp;amp;gl=US&quot;&gt;Monster Country&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Canadian owned and full-remote, we believe in giving small teams of talented people challenging problems and getting out of their way. That’s why we look for the best and brightest to join our team; people who have talent, vision, and commitment.&lt;/p&gt;
